# SASL is configured but the server has no sasl capability: say so and go on.
= auth sasl-plain
= account-password hunter2
= caps multi-prefix
> CAP LS 302
> NICK textual
> USER textual 0 * Textual
< :irc.example CAP * LS :multi-prefix
> CAP REQ multi-prefix
< :irc.example CAP * ACK multi-prefix
> CAP END
? notice SASL failed: the server does not offer SASL
< :irc.example 001 textual :Welcome
? registered textual
